"none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://uberblok.storagebits.workers.dev/"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_storagebits", "story_50180257", "show_hn", "front_page"], "author": "storagebits", "children": [50198204, 50198452, 50198924, 50198928, 50199189], "created_at": "2026-10-21T13:04:25Z", "created_at_i": 1792587865, "num_comments": 8, "objectID": "50180257", "points": 37, "story_id": 50180257, "story_text": "I&#x27;ve worked for a long time in the storage field during my career and ZFS is the piece of engineering I admire most in that space. I wanted a way to pay homage to it and to explore and better understand its internals. So I built Uberblok: a museum of ZFS. A deep dive into copy-on-write, txgs, vdevs, RAID-Z, snapshots, the ARC, metaslabs, the ZIL, send&#x2F;receive with explanations and animated diagrams.<p>I&#x27;m sure people here know these internals better than I do, so corrections are very welcome.<p>I built it with my agent swarm organization, Algotitan.<p>I hope you&#x27;ll enjoy the deep dive into Uberblok as much as I do.<p>Museum: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;uberblok.storagebits.workers.dev\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;uberblok.storagebits.workers.dev</a>\nRepo: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;algotitanhq&#x2F;uberblok\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;algotitanhq&#x2F;uberblok</a>", "title": "Show HN: Uberblok – an interactive museum of ZFS internals", "updated_at": "2026-10-22T18:52:22Z", "url": "https://uberblok.storagebits.workers.dev/"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "kiyouta"}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "VMMouse for NT 3.x: QEMU/VMware mouse integration driver"}, "url": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://github.com/rhargreaves/vmmouse-nt3"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_kiyouta", "story_50144727", "front_page"], "author": "kiyouta", "children": [50196253], "created_at": "2026-10-18T19:50:11Z", "created_at_i": 1792353011, "num_comments": 5, "objectID": "50144727", "points": 37, "story_id": 50144727, "title": "VMMouse for NT 3.x: QEMU/VMware mouse integration driver", "updated_at": "2026-10-22T18:55:23Z", "url": "https://github.com/rhargreaves/vmmouse-nt3"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "nimitmehra"}, "story_text": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "Dovepass answers one question for drone operators: given two points, can a drone legally fly between the two points?<p>I build route planning for delivery drivers and wanted to check what it would look like if the vehicle flies. Drone navigation is different from land-based vehicle navigation. In addition to road and traffic data, it requires data on buildings, building height, wind speed and direction, and total load, including the payload a drone might carry. It is also governed by a set of rules; depending on the area, federal, state, or county rules may apply.<p>The decision point becomes whether, at each point on the route the drone can fly based upon whether regulations permit, the wind direction favours it and whether it flying over a road or people? Depending on when the drone flies, the same path valid two hours ago may no longer be valid.<p>For example a trip from 24th &amp; Valencia ( Mission) to 19th Ave &amp; Irving (Inner Sunset) and back is 5.1 km each way. A DJI mini 4 Pro would take 19 min on 7 mph winds from the west and use 92% of its usable battery and give a Go signal with warning. But at 11mph wind from the same direction would become No-Go because it would use 111% of its usable battery. Or whenever there is a Giants game at Oracle Park, this route is unusable because it is 2.5miles from the stadium. FAA bars all drones within 3 nautical miles from a stadium from 1 hour before the game to one hour after it ends.<p>I chose San Francisco as the first city to build this because there is enough data about the buildings (92% coverage), wind data is easily available at the drone flying height, and the city has a mix of slopes, water bodies, buildings and airport-related airspace restrictions all in one city. The city also has local rules regarding drone flights in parks - both operated by the city as well as by Golden Gate National recreational areas ( National Park Service).<p>I used kimi to build it and claude acted a sa judge. To understand more about the challenges faced during the build and the tradeoffs made please read - <a href=\"https://dovepass.com/how-it-was-built/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://dovepass.com/how-it-was-built/</a>&quot;"}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "Show HN: Dovepass – can I legally fly a drone along this exact path in SF?"}, "url": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://dovepass.com"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_nimitmehra", "story_50156779", "show_hn", "front_page"], "author": "nimitmehra", "children": [50174672, 50174785, 50176120, 50199187], "created_at": "2026-10-19T19:21:56Z", "created_at_i": 1792437716, "num_comments": 8, "objectID": "50156779", "points": 27, "story_id": 50156779, "story_text": "Dovepass answers one question for drone operators: given two points, can a drone legally fly between the two points?<p>I build route planning for delivery drivers and wanted to check what it would look like if the vehicle flies. Drone navigation is different from land-based vehicle navigation. In addition to road and traffic data, it requires data on buildings, building height, wind speed and direction, and total load, including the payload a drone might carry. It is also governed by a set of rules; depending on the area, federal, state, or county rules may apply.<p>The decision point becomes whether, at each point on the route the drone can fly based upon whether regulations permit, the wind direction favours it and whether it flying over a road or people? Depending on when the drone flies, the same path valid two hours ago may no longer be valid.<p>For example a trip from 24th &amp; Valencia ( Mission) to 19th Ave &amp; Irving (Inner Sunset) and back is 5.1 km each way. A DJI mini 4 Pro would take 19 min on 7 mph winds from the west and use 92% of its usable battery and give a Go signal with warning. But at 11mph wind from the same direction would become No-Go because it would use 111% of its usable battery. Or whenever there is a Giants game at Oracle Park, this route is unusable because it is 2.5miles from the stadium. FAA bars all drones within 3 nautical miles from a stadium from 1 hour before the game to one hour after it ends.<p>I chose San Francisco as the first city to build this because there is enough data about the buildings (92% coverage), wind data is easily available at the drone flying height, and the city has a mix of slopes, water bodies, buildings and airport-related airspace restrictions all in one city. The city also has local rules regarding drone flights in parks - both operated by the city as well as by Golden Gate National recreational areas ( National Park Service).<p>I used kimi to build it and claude acted a sa judge. To understand more about the challenges faced during the build and the tradeoffs made please read - <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;dovepass.com&#x2F;how-it-was-built&#x2F;\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;dovepass.com&#x2F;how-it-was-built&#x2F;</a>&quot;", "title": "Show HN: Dovepass – can I legally fly a drone along this exact path in SF?", "updated_at": "2026-10-22T18:41:23Z", "url": "https://dovepass.com"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "brandonb"}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "AI analysis of CT scans finds 42.9% of patients have coronary inflammation"}, "url": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://www.biograph.com/newsroom/biograph-completes-first-u.s.-study-with-caristo-diagnostics%E2%80%99-ai-powered-c